Description: CVE-2026-62946 - Fix integer overflow in ReadJNXImage (coders/jnx.c)
 A crafted JNX image can specify a tile_length close to UINT_MAX. The value is
 later used in AcquireQuantumMemory((size_t) tile_length+2, ...). On systems
 where the addition wraps, this leads to an undersized allocation followed by a
 heap over-write (CWE-190 integer overflow leading to heap buffer overflow).
 This patch rejects tile_length values greater than UINT_MAX-2 before the
 allocation, throwing a ResourceLimitError instead.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/8018a5c3214ca9bf11a86c2816833dee920b1340
Bug: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-h22j-f9xw-xjjm
Author: ImageMagick Studio LLC
Last-Update: 2026-07-31
---
--- a/coders/jnx.c
+++ b/coders/jnx.c
@@ -289,6 +289,11 @@ static Image *ReadJNXImage(const ImageInfo *image_info,ExceptionInfo *exception)
           images=DestroyImageList(images);
           ThrowReaderException(CorruptImageError,"InsufficientImageDataInFile");
         }
+      if (tile_length > (UINT_MAX-2))
+        {
+          images=DestroyImageList(images);
+          ThrowReaderException(ResourceLimitError,"MemoryAllocationFailed");
+        }
       blob=(unsigned char *) AcquireQuantumMemory((size_t) tile_length+2,
         sizeof(*blob));
       if (blob == (unsigned char *) NULL)
Description: CVE-2026-62343 - Fix heap buffer over-write in morphology with invalid kernel
 A crafted kernel string or built-in kernel request with extreme dimensions
 could cause the kernel->width * kernel->height element count used to size the
 kernel->values allocation to overflow, producing an undersized buffer and a
 subsequent heap buffer over-write when the kernel values are populated.
 .
 This backports the upstream fix which introduces a new AcquireKernelValues()
 helper that validates the element count via HeapOverflowSanityCheckGetSize()
 before allocating, and routes every kernel->values allocation in
 ParseKernelArray(), AcquireKernelBuiltIn() and CloneKernelInfo() through it.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/b3a93f501011a8882ec4962dd6db9f0a71e6f050
Author: Cristy <urban-warrior@imagemagick.org>
Last-Update: 2026-07-31
