+# CVE-2026-61861 — False Positive for Debian 12 (bookworm)
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| **CVE ID** | CVE-2026-61861 |
+| **Component** | imagemagick |
+| **Distribution** | Debian 12 (bookworm) |
+| **Package version** | `imagemagick`, version `8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u13` |
+| **Upstream affected** | ImageMagick 7.x before 7.1.2-26; ImageMagick6 after 6.9.12-24 and before 6.9.13-51 |
+| **Assessment** | **FALSE POSITIVE — package is not vulnerable, no patch required.** |
+
+## Why this release is not affected
+
+CVE-2026-61861 is a use-after-free in `FormatMagickCaption` when memory
+allocation fails during caption reflow. Upstream introduced the vulnerable
+`ReplaceSpaceWithNewline()` helper in ImageMagick6 commit
+`1d597191bd1f45d05ff041c89b7e3f8759e9eaf5` (6.9.12-24). Debian bookworm
+ships 6.9.11.60, which predates that helper.
+
+Debian security tracker:
+
+* `[bookworm] - imagemagick <not-affected> (vulnerable code not present)`
+* bookworm and bookworm-security are both not-affected
+
+## Evidence
+
+```
+$ grep -n ReplaceSpaceWithNewline magick/annotate.c
+# no matches in 6.9.11.60
+```
+
+## Recommended action
+
+- Mark as `not_affected` / `vulnerable_code_not_present` in the scanner.
+
+## References
+
+- https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-61861
+- https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-qvxh-prvr-85w2
+- https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/1d597191bd1f45d05ff041c89b7e3f8759e9eaf5
+- https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/0091f38a106601893c77c2d298708048cd2930f5
